        <h2>Generator Maintenance Basics</h2>
        <p>Proper maintenance reduces fuel consumption and prevents costly breakdowns.</p>

        <h3>Daily Maintenance:</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Check oil level:</strong> Verify oil level before startup</li>
          <li><strong>Check coolant level:</strong> Ensure adequate cooling system fluid</li>
          <li><strong>Inspect air filter:</strong> Clean or replace as needed in dusty conditions</li>
          <li><strong>Check fuel level:</strong> Monitor fuel consumption and plan deliveries</li>
          <li><strong>Listen for unusual noises:</strong> Address problems before they become failures</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>Weekly Maintenance:</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Clean air filter:</strong> Replace or clean depending on conditions</li>
          <li><strong>Check belts and hoses:</strong> Look for cracks, fraying, or leaks</li>
          <li><strong>Test safety systems:</strong> Verify shutdown systems function properly</li>
          <li><strong>Check battery condition:</strong> Clean terminals and check electrolyte</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>Monthly Maintenance:</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Change engine oil:</strong> Use appropriate grade for operating conditions</li>
          <li><strong>Replace fuel filters:</strong> Prevent fuel contamination issues</li>
          <li><strong>Load bank test:</strong> Test generator at full load periodically</li>
          <li><strong>Check electrical connections:</strong> Tighten loose connections</li>
        </ul>

